# File: scripts/__tests__/execute-host.test.mjs, scripts/__tests__/sdlc-execute.test.mjs
# Generated from: specs/550-stop-the-sdlc-execute-controller-busy-waiting-while-a-stage-worker-waits-on-a-background-command/requirements.md
Feature: The execute controller blocks between polls while a worker waits behind its marker

  @SCN001
  Scenario: A settled worker behind a waiting marker does not spin the controller
    Given a stage worker whose agent record is idle with a waiting marker and no fresh handoff
    When the controller waits for that worker to resume
    Then every host poll is followed by a sleep of at least the host poll interval
    And the polls before the 60-second resume bound are bounded by the bound divided by the poll interval

  @SCN002
  Scenario: The worker's next turn is still observed promptly
    Given a stage worker waiting behind its marker
    When the worker starts a new turn and later writes a fresh handoff
    Then the controller observes the resumed turn within one host poll and returns that handoff

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Check-ins continue during the wait
    Given a worker waiting behind its marker for longer than the check-in interval
    When the interval elapses
    Then the controller issues the check-in report with the marker's command and age

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Existing settle and reminder behavior is preserved
    Given a settled worker whose marker is removed
    When the controller evaluates it
    Then the reminder or stop handling runs as before
    And waiting until working on an already-settled worker returns immediately
